+/* panel-clock-layer (arch-compositor-morph, T-215 census by fix-end-morph): the morph panel's countdown rolls its digit
+   strips ~25 times a second while the panel is open (JS 4328 rAF spring); unlayered, every roll frame repaints the
+   layer it paints into, the panel's veil layer (406 x 908 at m 1 in our Chrome card). Its own layer, sized to the clock, keeps
+   those repaints to the clock. The digits stay main-thread (cd-roll-ca). iOS WebKit only (-webkit-touch-callout is an
+   iOS-only property): WebKit snaps a layer to device pixels and paints its content at the renderer's subpixel offset
+   (RenderLayerBacking m_subpixelOffsetFromRenderer), so the glyphs keep their pixels; Chrome draws a new layer's text
+   up to 1 device px off (T2 edge 162-224 at m 1 in every layer variant), so Chrome keeps today's painting. */
+@supports (-webkit-touch-callout: none) {
+  .start-selling-morph-panel .waitlist-closing-countdown .countdown.svelte-1666oc5 {
+    transform: translateZ(0);
+  }
 }
